Z||000000||Pyric||12-17-2001||02:38 PM||||Well, I cranked my car this morning after fixing the EGR tube and replacing the vacuum lines and although the Idle is much steadier (1500rpms) the car still stalls.<P>At start it will crank and then stall 2 second later unless I give it some gas.  Then it will idle fine.  If I rev the engine and then quickly let off, it will stall or almost stall.<P>I've replaced (recently):<BR>the vacuum lines<BR>EGR tube<BR>EGR valve<BR>coolant temp sensor<BR>cold start sensor,<BR>vapor canister <BR>Throttle position sensor<BR>sparkplugs<BR>and (I was told by the previous owner) the Idle Air control.<P>oh, one more thing, the engine is brand new and it puts out a little white smoke right after it is cranked, but then again, it does have old gas in it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pyric||12-17-2001||04:59 PM||||Oh, almost forgot.  It's an 85 GT V6.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
